    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29561" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυστῠχ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unlucky, unfortunate</i>,
			of persons and things, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.87
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				832a
			</span></i>, etc.; freq. in Trag., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυστυχῆ πράσσειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					339
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. βίος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					602
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. εἴς τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1642
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τά τ᾽ ἔνδον τά τε θύραζε δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Or.</u>
					604
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ δυστυχές</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					913
				</span></i>
			. Adv.-
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1660
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				687e
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
